\oint_{\Gamma}\frac{|\Pi_r(p_*)|}{|z-p_*||\Pi_r(z)|}|dz|.
\end{equation}
Using the logarithmic potential theory in \cite{Saf2010}, we know that, if $z \notin [-1,1]$,
\[ \frac1r \log\frac{1}{|\Pi_r(z)|} = U^{\mu_r}(z)\]
which implies, as $\mu_r \overset{\ast}{\rightharpoonup} \mu$, that
\[ \lim_{r \rightarrow \infty} \frac1r \log\frac{1}{|\Pi_r(z)|} = U^{\mu}(z)\]
or equivalently
\[ \lim_{r \rightarrow \infty}  |\Pi_r(z)|^{\frac1r} = \exp(-U^{\mu}(z)).\]
This limit holds uniformly on compact sets outside $[-1,1]$.
If $p_* \in [-1,1]$, the situation is more delicate as $U^{\mu_r}(z)$ is not continuous on $[-1,1]$. For this purpose, we use \cite[Lem 1.6]{Saf2010} to guarantee that
\[ \liminf_{r \rightarrow \infty}\frac1r \log\frac{1}{|\Pi_r(z)|} \geq U^{\mu}(z) \]
\[ \limsup_{r \rightarrow \infty} {|\Pi_r(z)|^{\frac1r}} \leq \exp(-U^{\mu}(z)). \]
This implies that, given an $\varepsilon >0$, there exists $r_0>0$ such that for all $r \geq r_0$
\[\oint_{\Gamma}\frac{|\Pi_r(p_*)|}{|z-p_*||\Pi_r(z)|}|dz| \leq \frac{1}{dist(\Gamma,p_*)}\oint_{\Gamma}\exp( -r(U^{\mu_r}(p_*) - U^{\mu_r}(z))|dz| \leq\]
\[ \leq \frac{1}{dist(\Gamma,p_*)}|\Gamma|\exp( -r(U^{\mu}(p_*) - \max_{z \in \Gamma}U^{\mu}(z) - 2\varepsilon)).\]
Under our assumption, we can find an $\varepsilon_0$ such that for all $\varepsilon \leq \varepsilon_0$
\[ U^{\mu}(p_*) - \max_{z \in \Gamma}U^{\mu}(z) -2\varepsilon > 0. \]
This concludes the proof.

